{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/a10jqpsj","slide":2,"name":"Text 3","text":"Monitor resource utilization and workload of containerized applications.\nPredict future aggregate CPU utilization using Machine Learning.\nPerform reactive and predictive scaling of application replicas.\nDynamically manage healthy application replicas using Docker and Nginx.\nDetect persistent prediction errors and adapt the prediction model through validated retraining.\nEvaluate the system under different workload patterns.","textPreview":"Monitor resource utilization and workload of containerized applications. | Predict future aggregate CPU utilization using Machine Learnin...","textChars":426,"textLines":6,"bbox":[43.2,144,576,499.2]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/x4r21kru","slide":2,"name":"Text 4","text":"Abstract","textPreview":"Abstract","textChars":8,"textLines":1,"bbox":[657.6,100.8,576,38.4]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/w3i1sfa9","slide":2,"name":"Text 5","text":"The proposed system is a Docker-based predictive autoscaling framework that combines workload monitoring, machine learning-based CPU prediction, and automated replica management. A Random Forest regression model predicts future aggregate CPU utilization using current and historical workload metrics. A scaling controller uses the prediction to make scaling decisions, while Docker and Nginx dynamically manage application replicas. An error-aware adaptive mechanism is incorporated to retrain and validate the prediction model when persistent prediction errors are detected.","textPreview":"The proposed system is a Docker-based predictive autoscaling framework that combines workload monitoring, machine learning-based CPU pred...","textChars":575,"textLines":1,"bbox":[657.6,144,576,499.2]}
